# Fixed-width subtype scaling normalizes an in-range literal

Verifies the scaled magnitude folded while compiling agrees with the stored
value: `12cm` becomes `120mm`, which the declared `int8` representation can
hold, so the element is stored with the converted magnitude.

>>> source
let sizes: int8<mm>[] = [12cm]
print(sizes[0])

<<< stdout
120mm

<<< stderr
